course: dictionary
lesson: 14337
title: Words that block or hide
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An occlusion is a blocking or closing, where something gets in the way and stops something passing through or being seen. The word can mean different things in different subjects, so the context tells you which meaning is right. Read the words around it: they are the clues.
explain: «The doctor found an occlusion in the artery, so the blood could not flow freely.» The words doctor, artery and blood are clues: this is about a blockage in the body. Ask yourself: what is being blocked? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «The dentist checked her occlusion when she bit down.» Here it means how the top and bottom teeth fit together. «The Moon's occlusion of the star lasted for ten minutes.» In science, it means one object hiding another from view. Same word, different subject, different meaning.
explain: Weather maps can show occlusions too. Look for the clues, such as a cold front and a warm front meeting. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Occlusion means a blocking or closing of something.
fact: «Occlusion» in medicine means a blockage in a tube, pipe or blood vessel.
fact: «Occlusion» in dentistry means the way your top and bottom teeth fit together when you bite.
fact: «Occlusion» in weather means an occluded front, where a cold front catches up with a warm front.
fact: «Occlusion» in astronomy means one object hiding another from view, like the Moon passing in front of a star.
exercise: «The doctor found an occlusion in the artery, so the blood could not flow freely.» What does occlusion mean here? | A happy, cheerful mood | *A blockage that stops blood flowing | A kind of toothbrush | A bright light shining in the sky
exercise: «The dentist checked her occlusion when she bit down.» What is an occlusion in this sentence? | *The way the top and bottom teeth fit together | A hole in the gum | A new pair of braces | A sweet snack for after lunch
exercise: «The Moon's occlusion of the star lasted for ten minutes.» In science, what is happening? | The Moon is getting closer to the Earth | The star is growing bigger | *One object hides another from view | The star has gone out forever
test: «On the weather map, the occlusion showed where the cold front caught up with the warm front.» What does occlusion refer to here? | *An occluded front, where a cold front meets a warm front | Snow falling on the mountains | A hot, sunny day at the beach | A sudden clap of thunder
test: Which sentence uses occlusion to mean a blockage in a pipe? | «The bus was late again today.» | «The cat slept in the sunny window.» | «The children ate a big bowl of soup.» | *«The plumber found an occlusion in the pipe, so the water could not flow.»
exam: Which word is a good clue that occlusion is about teeth, not stars? | *Bite | Moon | Sky | Telescope
